<title>JAPAN: Japan September vehicle output up 7.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan September vehicle output up 7.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle production rose in September to 923,320 vehicles, up 7.3 percent from a year earlier, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>In the April to September period, vehicle production rose to 4,948,278 vehicles, up 0.3 percent from the same period a year earlier, the association said.</p>
<p>A breakdown of the figures with percentage changes follows:</p>
<p>					   SEP	     YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars				  704,525	     +10.1</p>
<p> Trucks				214,784	     -1.0</p>
<p> Buses				   4,011	     +1.4</p>
<p> Total				 923,320	     +7.3</p>
<p>					APR-SEP	    YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars				3,718,502	     +1.8</p>
<p> Trucks			    1,204,197	     -4.6</p>
<p> Buses				  25,579	    +17.6</p>
<p> Total			     4,948,278	     +0.3</p>
<p>Production by major manufacturers:</p>
<p>					     SEP	    YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Toyota Motor Corp	302,621	    +18.6</p>
<p> Nissan Motor Co Ltd    146,423	     -7.5</p>
<p> Mazda Motor Corp	  67,104	     +5.6</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors Corp 114,364	     +0.9</p>
<p> Honda Motor Co Ltd     100,734	    +27.3</p>
<p>					   APR-SEP	   YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Toyota Motor Corp    1,622,413	    +6.2 pct</p>
<p> Nissan Motor Co Ltd    784,201	    -5.8 pct</p>
<p> Mazda Motor Corp	 355,873	    -1.2 pct</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors Corp 566,304	   -12.8 pct</p>
<p> Honda Motor Co Ltd     526,764	    +11.2 pct</p>
</text>
